# N1 Answers – Project Setup and Package Management

## Purpose of package.json fields

**1. name**

The name field identifies the name of my Node.js project. It helps identify the project when managing packages.

**2. version**

The version field tells the current version of my project. It helps track changes and updates.

**3. description**

The description field provides a short explanation of what my project is about.

**4. main**

The main field specifies the main entry point of my project. In my activity, it is index.js.

**5. scripts**

The scripts field contains commands that I can run using npm. For example, I created a start script that runs my index.js file using npm start.

**6. dependencies**

Dependencies are packages my project needs to function. These packages are installed and used by my project.

**7. devDependencies**

DevDependencies are packages used mainly during development, such as tools that help me test or automatically restart my program while coding.

## What is node_modules?

The node_modules folder contains the packages and libraries installed through npm. These packages are needed by my project to use the functionality provided by other developers.

## Why is node_modules not included when submitting or sharing a project?

The node_modules folder is not included because it can be very large and contains packages that can be installed again using npm. Instead, package.json and package-lock.json record the dependencies so another user can install them by running npm install. This saves storage space and keeps the repository cleaner.